(* Pia.Math (#487): `sqrt` on f32 and f64 is proved correctly rounded by an
   integer algorithm over its bits, and compiled to `math.sqrt` by its
   @lower (ADR 0078), which LLVM makes one instruction; with --lower=off it
   is the algorithm. tests/std/math_test.c runs both against C's sqrtf and
   sqrt.
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %S/../../lib/Pia/math.goals
// RUN: piac --emit=core %S/../../lib/Pia/Math.pia | FileCheck --check-prefix=CORE %s
// RUN: piac --emit=llvm -O2 %S/../../lib/Pia/Math.pia | FileCheck --check-prefix=LLVM %s
// RUN: piac --emit=llvm -O2 --lower=off %S/../../lib/Pia/Math.pia | FileCheck --check-prefix=OFF %s
// RUN: piac --verify --trust-report --verify-only=sqrt %S/../../lib/Pia/Math.pia | FileCheck --check-prefix=TRUST %s
*)

(* The rounding theorems, the roots' bounds, the f64 root's loop invariant,
   and the interface's rounding contracts, for sqrt_soft and for sqrt.
// CHECK-NOT: failed
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:152:3: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:125:3: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:127:3: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:43:5: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:367:3: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:310:3: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:317:5: proved: the loop invariant holds after each iteration
// CHECK-DAG: Math.pia:62:5: proved: the postcondition holds
// CHECK: {{[0-9]+}} proved, 0 failed, 0 skipped

// CORE: math.sqrt %{{.*}} : f32
// CORE: math.sqrt %{{.*}} : f64

// LLVM: call float @llvm.sqrt.f32(
// LLVM: call double @llvm.sqrt.f64(

// OFF-NOT: llvm.sqrt

// TRUST: Math.pia:180:3: trusted: the lowering of 'sqrt(f32)' to MLIR (math.sqrt; sha256 {{[0-9a-f]+}})
// TRUST: Math.pia:420:3: trusted: the lowering of 'sqrt(f64)' to MLIR (math.sqrt; sha256 {{[0-9a-f]+}})
*)
